{
  "description": "DeviceCMYK colours (pdfnative 1.8 via generate_basic_pdf v1.7.0): every colour input takes a CMYK operand string 'C M Y K' (each 0.0–1.0) or a [c, m, y, k] ink-percentage tuple (0–100) beside its usual hex / RGB form — here the watermark, the header template, a link, an svg drawing, the table borders and the chart series. The content stream then paints with the `k` / `K` operators. For print, pair CMYK colours with a CMYK `outputIntent` (see pdfx4-cmyk-validate.json); under a PDF/A claim with the default sRGB intent the engine reports PDFA_DEVICE_CMYK_CONTENT. Self-contained: runs end-to-end with no placeholders.",
